:: ReadingRoom [karlowe] {"title":"02 / The Room That Reads You"}
# The room that reads you

READING ROOM / KARLOWE PASSAGE

Shelves rise into a ceiling painted with constellations that do not exist yet. A
small fire murmurs behind its grate. Every book has your name on its spine, but in a
different hand.

(if: $hasTea)[
  Your cup is still warm. Its steam bends toward a thin volume bound in grey wool.
](else:)[
  The room is cold without tea. Even the commas seem to shiver.
]

(if: $hasKey)[
  The brass key turns by itself on your palm. A book titled //Guests of the Last
  House// opens to a page that has been waiting for you.
](else:)[
  The final shelf has no handle—only a keyhole and the faint scent of honey.
]

|star-map>[
  The page shows a charcoal star-map. One mark is not a star, but a tiny square
  window sketched at the edge of everything.
]

(if: $insight < 2)[
  (link-repeat: "Read one line aloud")[(set: $insight to $insight + 1)
  The ink lifts like moths. Somewhere below, something taps once beneath the stairs.]
](else:)[
  **You understand:** the thing outside did not follow you here. The house called it,
  as it once called you.
]

(display: "Status")

(if: $hasKey)[
  (link-goto: "Take the warm key to the cellar", "Vault")
]

[[Return to the entrance->Start]]

